  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-16T13:39:50.753Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Idea: for big events, most users have someone with a desktop account that stands around as the room master to keep everything running and to have a client that only friends of this account can join (aka a bot account). Normally these account don't talk, don't move, and wear basic and/or highly performant avatars, which is all well and good but the  communication and presence in the room can cause just that little bit more lag in a high population room\nWhat I'm suggesting is haveing a headless( aka no render of the game and has no avatar) client which can start a world and allow users to auto join if they are a freind. This will also cut down on the requirements to have a good bot computer to run the game. This will also allow a larger volume of syncing and trigger proccessing to happen in the master headless client, and re-routeing it away from clients allowing them to have slightly better frames.\nEach bot would be linked to a vrc account as such: user Patrick has the bot Patrick-bot1, ect.",
